A recent experiment conducted by LHCb has made a precise calculation of a key parameter in the decay of $B^+ 	o K^+\mu^+ ar{
u_\mu}$. This parameter, denoted as $\phi_{B}^{cp}$, is a crucial indicator of $CP$-violating phenomena. By combining the results of this measurement with other observations, the experimenters have determined the value of this phase to be around $-0.0015$ with a margin of error. This is the most accurate measurement achieved so far in the field of $B$-physics. Furthermore, the experimenters have also investigated the relationship between the ratio of decay probabilities and the difference in mass-energetic properties of the $ ar{
u}_\mu$ and $
u_\mu}$ particles. This investigation has provided valuable insights into the characteristics of the $\lambda = (1 - 3\sqrt{3})$ parameter and the phase $\phi_{B}^{cp}$.
